General Conversion Methods
Any number can be converted from the scale of b to the scale of some integer b>=b, b>1, by using arithmetic operations in either the b-scale or the b-scale. Accordingly, there are four methods of conversion, depending on whether the number to be converted is an integer or a proper fraction.
